set_option autoImplicit false

/-!
Proposed kernel-authority assertions for the corrected source-aware mass-equivalent Rule-6 guard.
The assertions below require the kernel-only gate to reject `sorryAx`, native-evaluator trust and
project axioms; Lean's standard `propext`, `Classical.choice` and `Quot.sound` remain allowed.

The representation lemmas are generic in `AtomRepresentation`.  The `iodines_represent` and
`iodine_not_represent_bromine` instances are the frozen Rule-2 mass identity and a discrimination check.
The iodine fixture establishes an actual source graph automorphism, distinct physically bonded
ligand IDs, odd Fin4 ligand-position parity and transport of source-derived written root nodes.
It does not identify these nodes with returned occurrence cursors or prove the actual initial
partition is preserved. No concrete full Rule-6 guard witness or guarded production refusal is
asserted. The generic guard implication preserves the original center, partition and actual
root-transport clauses and explicitly requires all source Rule-2 masses known.

The complete executable Rules-1a--6 promoted pipeline for the five-atom source is **not** evaluated and
its conjectured orders/descriptor are **not** asserted here.  Scientific equivalence of ordinary `I`
and explicit `127I`, source adoption, scheduler integration and broader production admission remain
open and are not asserted.
-/

